  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Services obligated $2.4B in FY2026 to date across 343 awards, with an average award size of $7.1M. Amentum Services obligations fell 30.6% year over year. Amentum Services received $1.5B from the Department of Defense and $708M from the Department of Homeland Security, which together account for the bulk of federal buying. Amentum Services recorded notable activity in aviation support and security: Other Support Activities for Air Transportation totaled $853M and Security Guards and Patrol Services totaled $507M. Amentum Services also reported Engineering Services at $264M and Facilities Support Services at $222M. Amentum Services obligations by fiscal year show growth into FY24 and FY25 before the current-year partial total: FY21 was $1.4B, FY22 was $1.6B, FY23 was $2.5B, FY24 was $3.8B, and FY25 was $3.5B. Amentum Services has smaller totals in other markets such as Aircraft Manufacturing at $91M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $125M. The current-year totals are fiscal year to date and partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Amentum Services' obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B to Amentum Services in FY2026 to date, making it the largest buyer. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $708M. The remaining agencies include the Department of the Treasury at $81.9M, the General Services Administration at $72.4M, and smaller amounts from other agencies."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Amentum Services' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Other Support Activities for Air Transportation accounted for $853M of Amentum Services obligations, the largest single NAICS market. Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $507M and Engineering Services accounted for $264M. Facilities Support Services and Computer Facilities Management Services added $222M and $125M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
